{
  "content": "<p><strong>Instructor:</strong> Dennis Freeman</p>\n<p><strong>Description:</strong> Bode plots are a simpler method of graphing the frequency response, using the poles and zeros of the system to construct asymptotes for each segment on a log-log plot. The Q factor affects the sharpness of peaks and drop-offs in the system.</p>\n",
